//? Title: Sutherland-Hodgman: actual half-plane emissions and clipped walks
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Polygon clipping carries a complete subject walk through one rectangle
half-plane at a time. Actual inside/outside branches, intersection emissions and
post-phase walks retain the original triangle experiment.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For each closed-walk edge previous->current, both inside emits current; leaving
emits one crossing; entering emits crossing then current; both outside emits
nothing. Feed the actual output into left,right,bottom,top successively.
Boundaries count as inside and repeated points may remain. A convex subject
yields its convex clipped polygon. Concave subjects can represent disconnected
components through coincident bridge edges in a single output walk; this is not
a general multipolygon topology-repair operation. With four fixed boundaries the
total walk size/work is linear in input size, with a bounded constant expansion.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sutherland_hodgman_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/sutherland_hodgman.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::sutherland_hodgman_trace({{-1, 0}, {2, 0}, {0, 2}}, 0, 0, 1, 1);
    std::print("| actual boundary | previous | current | previous inside | current inside | actual emitted " "points |\n| ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | `{}` | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.boundary,
                   s.previous, s.current, s.previous_inside, s.current_inside,
                   s.emitted);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual triangle crossing unit viewport");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual crossing intersections",
                                     r.intersections));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual final walk vertices",
                                     r.polygon.size()));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/sutherland_hodgman_tiny.svg");
}
```
